  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Make the requested logarithm appear",
      "body": "<p>Take logarithms to base 3 of the supplied approximation. The identity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>k</mi><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mi>u</mi></mrow></math> lets you bring each exponent in front.</p>",
      "recap": "A common logarithm base turns powers into factors.",
      "pitfall": "Keep the base of the requested logarithm fixed.",
      "pause": "Apply the rule on both sides, then isolate the logarithm you need.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l06",
          "reminder": "Use the logarithm laws before attempting a numerical approximation."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>&#x02248;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></math> implies <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x02248;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>. Therefore <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x02248;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mrow></math>. <strong>Answer A.</strong></p><p>It lies between 0 and 1, as required by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></math>.</p>",
